        "next_image_read": null,
        "content": [
          "\\begin{theorem}\\label{three:thm:main}\nLet $\\alpha>0$. For every sufficiently small $\\tau>0$, depending\non $\\alpha$, and every $0<\\nu\\le\\tau$, there exist $\\eps>0$ and\n$n_0\\in\\mathbb N$ for which the following holds. Let $G$ be a\ngraph of order $n\\ge n_0$, with $\\Delta(G)\\le k$ and $k\\ge\\alpha n$.\nSuppose\n\\[\n V(G)=U_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup U_q\\cup Z,\\qquad q\\in\\{1,2,3\\},\n \\qquad |U_i|\\ge\\alpha n,\\qquad a+|Z|+1\\le\\eps n,\n\\]\nand each $G[U_i]$ contains a spanning robust $(\\nu,\\tau)$-expander\nof minimum degree at least $k-a$. If $G$ has no $k$-overfull set,\nthen $G$ is $k$-edge-colorable.\n\\end{theorem}"
        ]
      }
